# Comprehensive Backend Architecture Audit Report

This report presents a thorough, read-only audit of the entire SafePulse backend codebase, covering all modules owned by **Person 1** (SOS, Guardians, Calling, Escalation, Responders), **Person 2** (Safety Session, Location, Ride Monitoring, Safe Places, Crime Map, Transport), and **Person 3** (Auth, Users, Voice Threat Analysis, Audio Storage, RAG Safety Assistant).

---

## 1. Module Analysis (Items 1–15 per Module)

### 1. `sos` (`src/modules/sos/`)
1. **Purpose:** Central SOS state machine (`VERIFYING` → `ACTIVE` → `GUARDIAN` → `NEARBY_RESPONDER` → `EMERGENCY_SERVICE` / `POLICE` / `RESOLVED` / `CANCELLED`).
2. **APIs/Routes:** `POST /api/v1/sos`, `GET /api/v1/sos/active`, `GET /api/v1/sos/history`, `GET /api/v1/sos/:id`, `GET /api/v1/sos/:id/escalation`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/confirm`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/cancel`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/acknowledge`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/resolve`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/escalation/start`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/responders/notify`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/responders/:responderId/acknowledge`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/escalation/acknowledge`, `POST /api/v1/sos/:id/escalation/police`.
3. **Models Used:** `SosEvent` (`sosEvents` collection), references [User](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/tests/guardian.endpoint.test.js#46-48), `SafetySession`.
4. **Utilities Used:** [ApiError](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/ApiError.js#1-35), [asyncHandler](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/asyncHandler.js#1-3), `response` ([sendSuccess](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/response.js#1-3), [sendCreated](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/response.js#4-5), [sendError](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/response.js#6-10)), [emitToUserRoom](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/index.js#28-54) ([sockets/index.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/index.js)), [isUserOnline](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/index.js#55-69).
5. **External Services Used:** None directly (relies on LiveKit/Police via adjacent services).
6. **Socket.IO Events Emitted:** `sos:verification-required`, `sos:confirmed`, `sos:cancelled`, `sos:timeout`, `sos:activated`, `sos:guardian-notified`, `sos:guardian-acknowledged`, `sos:escalating`, `sos:resolved`, `sos:guardian:notify`, `sos:responder:notify`, `sos:police:escalated`, `sos:guardian:acknowledged`, `sos:responder:acknowledged`, `responder:sos-notification`, `responder:sos-acknowledged`, `responder:sos-expired`. Listens to: None directly (triggered via REST / safetyEventBus bridge).
7. **Internal Events Emitted/Listens:** Emits/Listens via in-memory timer callbacks for verification and escalation timeouts.
8. **Modules Imported:** `guardians`, `calling`, `responders`, [police](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.events.js#575-592).
9. **Modules Depending on It:** `webhooks` (indirectly), `safetyEventBus` consumers.
10. **Internal Functionality:** Verification timer Map, atomic MongoDB state transitions, escalation step resolution, responder notification broadcast.
11. **Duplicated Functionality:** None within Person 1; however, Person 3's `groqThreat` endpoint returns `sosTriggered: boolean` without posting to this module.
12. **Imports/Exports Status:** Intact ES modules.
13. **Environment Variables Required:** `MONGODB_URI`, `GUARDIAN_ESCALATION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, `RESPONDER_ESCALATION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`.
14. **npm Dependencies Required:** `mongoose`, `express`, `zod`.
15. **Assumptions About Other Modules:** Assumes `SafetySession` exists if `safetySessionId` provided; assumes [User](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/tests/guardian.endpoint.test.js#46-48) exists for emergency settings.

