### 3. `calling` (`src/modules/calling/`)
1. **Purpose:** Manages browser-to-browser emergency calls and LiveKit room token generation.
2. **APIs/Routes:** `POST /api/v1/calls/start`, `POST /api/v1/calls/token`, `POST /api/v1/calls/:id/accept`, `POST /api/v1/calls/:id/reject`, `POST /api/v1/calls/end`.
3. **Models Used:** [Call](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/calling/call.service.js#492-566) (`calls` collection), `SosEvent`, [User](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/tests/guardian.endpoint.test.js#46-48), [Guardian](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/guardians/guardian.service.js#69-77).
4. **Utilities Used:** [ApiError](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/ApiError.js#1-35), [asyncHandler](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/asyncHandler.js#1-3), `response`, [emitToUserRoom](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/index.js#28-54).
5. **External Services Used:** `livekit-server-sdk` (`AccessToken`).
6. **Socket.IO Events Emitted:** `call:outgoing`, `call:ringing`, `call:accepted`, `call:rejected`, `call:connected`, `call:disconnected`, `call:failed`, `call:ended`.
7. **Internal Events:** None.
8. **Modules Imported:** `guardians` (queries guardians directly in repository).
9. **Modules Depending on It:** `webhooks` (updates Call model based on LiveKit callbacks).
10. **Internal Functionality:** Token minting, atomic call state machine (`OUTGOING` → `RINGING` → `ACCEPTED` → `CONNECTED` → `ENDED`).
11. **Duplicated Functionality:** None.
12. **Imports/Exports Status:** Intact ES modules.
13. **Environment Variables:** `LIVEKIT_URL`, `LIVEKIT_API_KEY`, `LIVEKIT_API_SECRET`, `LIVEKIT_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS`.
14. **npm Dependencies:** `livekit-server-sdk`, `mongoose`, `express`, `zod`.
15. **Assumptions About Other Modules:** Assumes an active `SosEvent` exists for starting an emergency call.

