## 2. Module Map (A)

```text
sos → Central SOS state & escalation → sos.routes.js, sos.service.js, sos.repository.js, sos.model.js → /api/v1/sos/* → startGuardianEscalation, startResponderEscalation, escalateToPolice → guardians, calling, responders, police, sockets

guardians → Guardian invites & priority → guardian.routes.js, guardian.service.js, guardian.repository.js, guardian.model.js → /api/v1/guardians/* → createGuardian, acceptGuardian, rejectGuardian → calling, User, sockets

calling → WebRTC emergency calling → call.routes.js, call.service.js, call.repository.js, call.model.js → /api/v1/calls/* → startEmergencyCall, createCallToken, acceptCall, rejectCall, endCall → guardians, livekit-server-sdk, sockets

location → GPS ping ingestion & history → location.routes.js, location.service.js, location.model.js → /api/v1/location/* → recordPoint, getHistory → safetySession, monitoring

ride → Ride creation, OCR & route tracking → ride.routes.js, ride.service.js, ride.model.js → /api/v1/rides/* → confirmRide, startRide, stopRide → googleMaps, safetySession, sockets

monitoring → Detection of off-route & long-stop → monitoring.service.js, routeMonitor.service.js, stopDetector.service.js → None (internal) → evaluateRidePoint, checkOffRoute, checkLongStop → safetyEventBus, ride.model

voice → Threat scoring & audio recordings → voice.routes.js, voice.controller.js, voiceRecording.model.js → /api/v1/voice/* → analyzeVoice, recordVoiceRecording → groqThreat, geminiTranslate, cloudinary

assistant → RAG safety chatbot → assistant.routes.js, assistant.controller.js, chatSession.model.js, chatMessage.model.js → /api/v1/assistant/chat → chat → geminiChat, jinaEmbedding, vectorStore

webhooks → LiveKit voice state sync → webhook.routes.js, webhook.service.js, webhook.controller.js → /api/v1/webhooks/livekit → handleLiveKitEvent → call.repository, calling.events
```

---

## 3. Actual Dependency Graph (B)

```text
sos → guardians
  Why: sos.service requires guardian records to build Escalation Level 1 (Guardian Stage).
  Which function/file: escalation.service.js -> startGuardianEscalation() calls guardianRepository.findActiveGuardians().
  Equivalent functionality: None.

sos → calling
  Why: sos.service requires user profiles to resolve display names for socket event payloads.
  Which function/file: sos.service.js -> acknowledgeSOS() calls callRepository.findUserById().
  Equivalent functionality: Duplicate user lookup logic exists in guardian.dependencies.js.

calling → guardians
  Why: calling.service requires checking if a guardian account is active before starting an emergency call.
  Which function/file: call.service.js -> selectGuardian() calls callRepository.findActiveGuardians().
  Equivalent functionality: Duplicated repository query.

location → safetySession
  Why: location.service updates the last known GPS coordinate on the parent safety session.
  Which function/file: location.service.js -> recordPoint() calls safetySession.service.updateLastLocation().
  Equivalent functionality: None.

location → monitoring
  Why: location.service triggers route/stop detection when a ping has an associated rideId.
  Which function/file: location.service.js -> recordPoint() calls monitoring.service.evaluateRidePoint().
  Equivalent functionality: None.

monitoring → safetyEventBus
  Why: monitoring.service emits detected safety anomalies (OFF_ROUTE, LONG_STOP) for system-wide consumption.
  Which function/file: routeMonitor.service.js & stopDetector.service.js call safetyEventBus.emitSafetyEvent().
  Equivalent functionality: None.

webhooks → calling
  Why: LiveKit webhook service updates the internal Call state machine when WebRTC media connects/disconnects.
  Which function/file: webhook.service.js calls call.repository functions (markConnected, markEndedFromWebhook, markFailedFromWebhook).
  Equivalent functionality: None.
```

---

## 4. Duplicate Functionality (C)

1. **Duplicate Socket.IO Initialization & Handlers:**
   - Person 1 uses [src/sockets/index.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/index.js) + [src/sockets/authSocket.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/authSocket.js) ([emitToUserRoom](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/index.js#28-54)).
   - Person 2 uses `src/socket/socket.js` ([emitToUser](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/authSocket.js#44-48), `emitToRide`, `emitToSession`).
   - *Risk:* Two different socket initialization pathways and room naming standards exist in the same codebase.

2. **Duplicate Transport Search Services:**
   - Person 2 has `src/modules/transport/` (`/api/v1/transport/search` using Google Places).
   - Person 3 has `src/modules/person 3 services/tavilyTransport.service.js` (`/api/v1/emergency/transport/search` using Tavily + Gemini).
   - *Risk:* Two unlinked transport endpoints with different route signatures.

3. **Duplicate User Profile / Account Lookups:**
   - [sos.dependencies.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.dependencies.js), [guardian.dependencies.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/guardians/guardian.dependencies.js), and [call.repository.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/calling/call.repository.js) all contain separate Mongoose queries for `User.findById()`.

4. **Duplicate Error Handlers:**
   - Person 1 & 2 use [src/middleware/errorHandler.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/middleware/errorHandler.js) + [ApiError.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/ApiError.js).
   - Person 3 modules use custom error response helpers ([badRequest(res, code, message)](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/ApiError.js#11-14)) inline inside [voice.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/voice/voice.controller.js) and [assistant.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/assistant/assistant.controller.js).

5. **Duplicate Cloudinary Setup:**
   - Person 2 has `src/integrations/cloudinary/cloudinary.js`.
   - Person 3 has `src/modules/person 3 services/cloudinary.service.js`.

---

## 5. Integration Risks (D)

1. **Syntax Mismatch (ESM vs CommonJS):**
   - [package.json](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/package.json) specifies `"type": "module"`.
   - All Person 1 & Person 2 modules use ES module syntax (`import`/`export`).
   - Person 3 modules ([voice.routes.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/voice/voice.routes.js), [voice.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/voice/voice.controller.js), [assistant.routes.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/assistant/assistant.routes.js), [assistant.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/assistant/assistant.controller.js)) use CommonJS syntax ([require](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/middleware/auth.js#16-38)/`module.exports`).
   - *Impact:* Server boot will crash with `ReferenceError: require is not defined in ES module scope` if Person 3 routes are mounted directly.

2. **Unconnected Safety Event Bus (SOS Trigger Gap):**
   - Person 2 emits `OFF_ROUTE` and `LONG_STOP` to `safetyEventBus`.
   - Person 3 returns `sosTriggered: true` from `/api/v1/voice/analyze` but does NOT emit to `safetyEventBus`.
   - [sos.service.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.service.js) has no listener registered on `safetyEventBus` to automatically call [createSOS()](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.service.js#166-253).
   - *Impact:* Automated detections (Voice Danger, Off Route, Long Stop) stay completely isolated and never auto-create an SOS in `VERIFYING` state.

3. **Database Collection Naming Mismatch:**
   - Person 1 models use explicit `collection: 'sosEvents'`, `collection: 'guardians'`, `collection: 'calls'`.
   - Person 3 models use default Mongoose pluralization (`chatsessions`, `chatmessages`, `knowledgechunks`, `voicerecordings`).

4. **Missing Route Mounts in [app.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/app.js):**
   - [app.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/app.js) currently only mounts Person 1 routes (`/api/v1/sos`, `/api/v1/guardians`, `/api/v1/calls`, `/api/v1/responders`, `/api/v1/webhooks`).
   - Person 2 routes (`/safety-sessions`, `/location`, `/rides`, `/safe-places`, `/crime`, `/transport`) and Person 3 routes (`/voice`, `/assistant`) are completely unmounted.

---

## 6. End-to-End Flow Problems (E)

1. **Flow 1: Ride → Safety Session → Monitoring → Voice → SOS**
   - *Broken Link:* [monitoring.service.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/monitoring/monitoring.service.js) emits `OFF_ROUTE` to `safetyEventBus`, but [sos.service.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.service.js) never subscribes to `safetyEventBus`.
   - *Broken Link:* [voice.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/voice/voice.controller.js) analyzes voice threat via Groq, but does not emit `VOICE_DANGER` to `safetyEventBus` or invoke [createSOS()](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.service.js#166-253).

2. **Flow 2: SOS → Guardian → Responders → Police**
   - *Intact Internal Mechanics:* Person 1's internal escalation chain (`VERIFYING` → `ACTIVE` → `GUARDIAN` → `NEARBY_RESPONDER` → `POLICE`) is 100% complete and fully verified via tests.

3. **Flow 3: Guardian Request → Accept/Reject**
   - *Intact Internal Mechanics:* Person 1's guardian request and accept/reject flows are 100% complete and bound to socket notifications.

4. **Flow 4: Guardian Transport → Location**
   - *Broken Link:* Person 3's `/api/v1/emergency/transport/search` expects victim/guardian coordinates, but does not pull live coordinates from Person 2's [location.service.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/location/location.service.js) or `LocationPoint` collection.

---

## 7. Recommended Integration Plan (F)

### Priority P0: Fix Server Startup & Module Mismatches
1. Refactor Person 3 CommonJS files ([voice.routes.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/voice/voice.routes.js), [voice.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/voice/voice.controller.js), [assistant.routes.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/assistant/assistant.routes.js), [assistant.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/assistant/assistant.controller.js), and associated services/models) to standard ES Module syntax (`import`/`export`).
2. Consolidate Socket.IO initializers ([src/sockets/index.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/sockets/index.js) vs `src/socket/socket.js`) into a single unified socket gateway.
3. Mount all Person 2 and Person 3 routes in [src/app.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/app.js).

### Priority P1: Connect Cross-Module Safety Event Bus
1. Connect `safetyEventBus` to [sos.service.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.service.js) by registering an [onSafetyEvent](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/safetyEventBus.js#56-61) listener that automatically calls [createSOS()](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/sos/sos.service.js#166-253) with `triggerType: event.type` (`OFF_ROUTE`, `LONG_STOP`, `GEOFENCE_BREACH`).
2. Update [voice.controller.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/voice/voice.controller.js) so that when `threatLevel > 50`, it emits a standardized `VOICE_DANGER` safety event onto `safetyEventBus`.

### Priority P2: Correct Business Behavior & Endpoint Alignment
1. Wire Person 3's emergency transport search endpoint (`/api/v1/emergency/transport/search`) to automatically query Person 2's [location.service.js](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/modules/location/location.service.js) for the latest victim/guardian coordinates if explicit coordinates are omitted.
2. Unify error handling across Person 3 controllers by adopting [ApiError](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/ApiError.js#1-35) and [asyncHandler](file:///d:/kolkata%20hackathon/Backend/src/utils/asyncHandler.js#1-3).

### Priority P3: Cleanup & Refactoring
1. Deduplicate Cloudinary utility modules (`src/integrations/cloudinary/` vs `src/modules/person 3 services/cloudinary.service.js`).
2. Align collection names and indexes across all models.
